there's a new cronyism allegation  against the health secretary  matt hancock it concerns some shares  he's been given in a family firm which  has been doing business with the  national health service it is being  claimed he hasn't properly declared it  the government insists he has though now  mr hancock was given some shares in a  company called  topwood it's owned by his sister  and also other family members now he  declared the shares in the earlier this  week in the register of members interest  um and at the time it was thought the  company had just been doing business  with the nhs in wales  now it's emerged according to the health  service journal  that the company's been doing business  with the national health service in  england uh for which of course mr  hancock is responsible  as health secretary though he isn't  responsible for the nhs in wales  uh it is being claimed that he  didn't state in ministerial declarations  that his sister  and other family members owned the firm  uh jonathan  ashworth the shadow health secretary has  tweeted  shocking but sadly i suspect no one is  surprised anymore  at the cronyism at the heart of this  government  well a spokesman for the the health  secretary said that  he's acted entirely properly all  declarations of interest have been made  in accordance with the mineral  ministerial code ministers have no  involvement in the awarding of these  contracts  no conflict of interest arises uh it's  being  said by the department that he wasn't  involved  um he checked with the permanent  secretary  whether there are any conflicts of  interest and the department is saying  these shareholdings are only known about  because he's followed the transparency  rules in the full and correct way  john craig updating us there from  westminster thank you
 

